      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T23:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, technically `dartmonkey` doesn\u0027t have it. But since `bloonchipper` and `helipilot` do have it, I think it makes sense to share it for those boards. When we add `dartmonkey`, we probably just need to conditionally select the version of `get_fp_transport_type` that we use. One way to do it would be something like:\n\n```\nzephyr_library_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_EC_HOST_CMD \"fp_transport.c\")\n```\n\n```\nzephyr_library_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_HAS_UART_SPI_TRANSPORT \"fp_transport_uart_spi.c\")\nzephyr_library_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_HAS_SPI_TRANSPORT_ONLY \"fp_transport_spi.c\")\n```\n\nwhere `CONFIG_HAS_UART_SPI_TRANSPORT` is set for `bloonchipper`/`helipilot` and `CONFIG_HAS_SPI_TRANSPORT_ONLY` is set for `dartmonkey`.",
      "parentUuid": "c1b2a3ba_d70442aa",
      "revId": "1a74e94c924fc1470350dab3f7b2debd5cae73a6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
